      ],
      "impact": "The EPD boost/charge-pump circuit may not operate correctly due to insufficient capacitance and lower voltage rating, potentially causing display malfunction or capacitor failure.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["C11"],
      "pins": ["C11.1"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(C11-Pad1)", "GND"],
      "observed": "C11 is a 0.1uF capacitor with pin 1 on the net unconnected-(C11-Pad1) (no other nodes) and pin 2 on GND. Its footprint is Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder, an inductor footprint.",
      "expected": "C11 should be connected between a supply rail and GND (e.g., as a decoupling capacitor) and use a capacitor footprint.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"59\") (name \"unconnected-(C11-Pad1)\") (node (ref \"C11\") (pin \"1\")"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"C11\") (value \"0.1uF\") (footprint \"Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder\")"}
      ],
      "impact": "C11 provides no decoupling or filtering; if it was intended to stabilize a rail, that rail may be noisy. The wrong footprint may also prevent proper assembly.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "short_to_ground",
      "components": ["U5"],
      "pins": ["U5.13", "U5.14"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "U5 pins 13 and 14 (LAN_PORT3_TX+ and LAN_PORT3_TX-) are both connected to the GND net.",
      "expected": "Unused Ethernet TX differential pins should not be shorted to ground; they should be left unconnected or properly terminated.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"13\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT3_TX+\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"14\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT3_TX-\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"}
      ],
      "impact": "If the SKW92A Ethernet PHY is active, shorting TX outputs to ground could cause excessive current or damage the module. At minimum, it is not standard practice for unused differential pairs.",
      "confidence": 0.7
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain several anomalies: C1 has the wrong value (0.1uF/16V instead of 1uF/25V), C11 is an unconnected capacitor with an inductor footprint, and U5 Ethernet TX pins 13/14 are shorted to ground."
}

